    {
        "id": "27881117b41f99e0",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "8f708038682bad2f",
        "name": "Arduino (2)",
        "info": "| Trigger / Context             | Topic             | Message     | Notes                                       |\n| ----------------------------- | ----------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------- |\n| BLE LED turned ON             | 2474042/feeds/led | #close      | Indicates the lock/window closed            |\n| BLE LED turned OFF            | 2474042/feeds/led | #away       | Indicates LED is OFF                        |\n| Web keypad '*' pressed        | 2474042/feeds/led | <position>  | Sends current entered number for validation |\n| Physical keypad '*' pressed   | 2474042/feeds/led | !<position> | Sends current entered number for validation |\n\n\n\n| Expected Message   | Topic             | Notes                                        |\n| ------------------ | ----------------- | -------------------------------------------- |\n| #correctPassword   | 2474042/feeds/led | Unlock the lock; triggers LCD update         |X\n| #incorrectPassword | 2474042/feeds/led | Wrong password; triggers LCD animation/reset |X\n| #WIN_0             | 2474042/feeds/led | Sets windowStatus = 0                        |X\n| #WIN_1             | 2474042/feeds/led | Sets windowStatus = 1                        |X\n| #WIN_2             | 2474042/feeds/led | Sets windowStatus = 2                        |X\n| #WIN_3             | 2474042/feeds/led | Sets windowStatus = 3                        |X\n| #DOOR              | 2474042/feeds/led | Does something idk                           |X\n\n\nIf its \"checked (X)\" it means that node red has the nodes to do it (scroll for the top one -->). ",
        "x": 140,
        "y": 320,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "7e618e0a5f9354dc",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "8f708038682bad2f",
        "name": "X - Arduino (1) - X",
        "info": "Ce Arduino n'utilise pas lq MQTT par contre il envoie du BT aux Arduino (2), qui envoie lui\nmeme du MQTT.\n\n\nFrom Arduino (2):\n\n| Trigger / Context             | Topic             | Message     | Notes                                       |\n| ----------------------------- | ----------------- | ----------- | ------------------------------------------- |X\n| BLE LED turned ON             | 2474042/feeds/led | #close      | Indicates the lock/window closed            |*\n| BLE LED turned OFF            | 2474042/feeds/led | #away       | Indicates LED is OFF   \n\nIt sends it to Arduino (2), and then Arduino (2) takes care of the rest.",
        "x": 170,
        "y": 260,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "c737cb18e681702f",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "8f708038682bad2f",
        "name": "Photon (1)",
        "info": "| Message Payload | Topic                   | Action / Notes                           |\n| --------------- | ----------------------- | ---------------------------------------- |\n| buzzerPulse     | cak47/Feeds/Ampoulelock | Short buzzer pulse                       |\n| buzzerLong      | cak47/Feeds/Ampoulelock | Turns on long buzzer alert (`alerte=1`)  |\n| buzzerBuzz      | cak47/Feeds/Ampoulelock | Continuous \"earrape\" buzzer (`alerte=2`) |\n| buzzerOff       | cak47/Feeds/Ampoulelock | Turn off buzzer (`alerte=0`)             |\n| ampoule         | cak47/Feeds/Ampoulelock | Turn ON lamp/ampoule                     |\n| ampouleOff      | cak47/Feeds/Ampoulelock | Turn OFF lamp/ampoule                    |\n| #unlock         | cak47/Feeds/Ampoulelock | Unlock the lock (digital HIGH on `lock`) |\n\n\nThis Photon only receives!",
        "x": 140,
        "y": 380,
        "wires": []
    },
    {
        "id": "06f3cb0698dbf1a5",
        "type": "comment",
        "z": "8f708038682bad2f",
        "name": "Photon (2)",
        "info": "| Trigger / Context                 | Topic             | Message         | Notes                   |\n| --------------------------------- | ----------------- | --------------- | ----------------------- |\n| RFID card detected                | 2474042/feeds/led | Card UID in HEX | Example: `04A3B21C`     |\n| Window sensor state change (both) | 2474042/feeds/led | #WIN_0          | Both windows closed     |(unused, useless)\n| Window sensor state change        | 2474042/feeds/led | #WIN_1          | Left closed, Right open |\n| Window sensor state change        | 2474042/feeds/led | #WIN_2          | Left open, Right closed |\n| Window sensor state change        | 2474042/feeds/led | #WIN_3          | Both windows open       |\n\nThis Photon only sends! \n(Sroll -->)",
        "x": 140,
        "y": 440,
        "wires": []
    },
